    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "**n8n Workflow: Image-to-Video Preparation with Dimension Restriction**\n\n**Purpose:**\nThis workflow handles images uploaded to a Google Drive folder, resizes them to specific dimensions (width & height) for API video generation, and processes them through Telegram and Google Sheet logging.\n\n**Flow Steps:**\n\n**Trigger:**\n\nActivated when a user uploads an image to a specific Google Drive folder.\n\n**HTTP Request Node:**\n\nRetrieves the uploaded image from Google Drive.\n\nConverts the image into binary data for further processing.\n\n**Edit Image Node:**\n\nResizes the image to the specified width and height (to comply with API video generation restrictions).\n\n**Upload Edited Image:**\n\nThe resized image is uploaded to the same Google Drive folder as the original file.\n\n**Delete Original File:**\n\nAfter successful upload of the resized image, the original file is deleted from Google Drive.\n\n**Telegram Node:**\n\nSends the resized image to the n8n-created Telegram bot.\n\n**Google Sheet Logging:**\n\nLogs the uploaded image into a Google Sheet for record keeping.\n\n**Notes:**\n\nEnsures all images meet the API's dimension requirements.\n\nKeeps Google Drive organized by removing originals after resizing.\n\nFully automates sending images to Telegram and logging activity.",
        "height": 1024,
        "width": 496
      },
